  <title id="bdl25featurewarping-title">Successive warping of a two-dimensional input loop by a deep GP</title>
  <desc id="bdl25featurewarping-desc">Top row: points on a circle in the input space x1, x2 are mapped through three successive Gaussian process layers with an exponentiated quadratic covariance function; the loop is folded and twisted, and the deformation created in the first layer is carried into the next layers and transformed further. Bottom row: the same circle mapped through three layers with a linear covariance function; each layer only stretches and rotates it into an ellipse, which flattens toward a line.</desc>
